<title>UK: RUGBY UNION-LEICESTER BEAT TOULOUSE IN EUROPEAN CUP SEMIFINAL.</title>
<headline>RUGBY UNION-LEICESTER BEAT TOULOUSE IN EUROPEAN CUP SEMIFINAL.</headline>
<dateline>LEICESTER, England 1997-01-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Leicester beat Toulouse</p>
<p>of France 37-11 (halftime 20-6) in a European Cup semifinal on</p>
<p>Saturday.</p>
<p>Scores:</p>
<p>Leicester - Tries: Neil Back, Darren Garforth, Steve</p>
<p>Hackney, Austin Healy, penalty try. Conversions: John Liley (3).</p>
<p>Penalties: Liley (2).</p>
<p>Toulouse - Try: Michel Marfaing. Penalties: Christophe</p>
<p>Deylaud (2).</p>
<p>Second semifinal: Brive (France) v Cardiff (Wales), In</p>
<p>Brive, on Sunday</p>
</text>
